<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		This file exists for one key. Every other Info.plist value for this target still comes
		from GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE and the INFOPLIST_KEY_ build settings, which Xcode merges
		into this file at build time; NSBonjourServices is an array, and the INFOPLIST_KEY_
		mechanism carries strings and booleans only. It sits beside the target's folder rather
		than inside it because a synchronized root group copies its own files into the bundle,
		and Xcode 26 cannot read a project whose exception set is attached to a target's own
		synchronized root group; the Mac target's exception list, which already names every
		ThreadingMobile file, is the one mechanism that works for both.

		Without it, browsing for the service fails silently on iOS 14 and later: no results, no
		error, no prompt. MobileLocalNetworkPermissionTests asserts the built app carries it,
		because "silently finds nothing" is not a symptom anybody debugs quickly.
	-->
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_threading._tcp</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
